    "answer": {
      "short": "$V_{\\text{sphere}}=\\frac{4}{3}\\pi r^3$.",
      "worked": "The sphere fits perfectly, so $h=2r$.\n$$\\begin{align*}V_{\\text{sphere}}&=V_{\\text{cylinder}}-V_{\\text{cone}}\\\\V_{\\text{sphere}}&=\\pi r^2h-\\frac{1}{3}\\pi r^2h\\\\V_{\\text{sphere}}&=\\frac{2}{3}\\pi r^2h\\\\V_{\\text{sphere}}&=\\frac{2}{3}\\pi r^2(2r)\\\\V_{\\text{sphere}}&=\\frac{4}{3}\\pi r^3\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
